        "The model sits behind a port. That means pipelines and agents call a small internal interface such as 'classify this text' or 'draft this rule', and an adapter decides whether Bedrock or a Databricks model serves it. Swapping models or providers is then a configuration change, not a rewrite. Databricks AI Gateway can sit in front of external models, including Bedrock, to add rate limits, usage logging and guardrails in one place.",
